Adding a secondary light source, such as a reflector, can indeed help to even out the lighting and reduce shadows. A reflector can be used to bounce light onto the side of your face, filling in any areas that might be in shadow and creating a more balanced look. However, be cautious not to overdo it, as too much fill light can flatten the image and reduce depth. A subtle use of a reflector can help to enhance the overall lighting and create a more polished, professional look.

